<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Cumnock Coal appoints new chairman.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Cumnock Coal appoints new chairman.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cumnock Coal Ltd said on Tuesday that former alternate director Stanley Howard has been elected a director and chairman of the company.</p>
<p>His appointment follows the resignation last Wednesday of chairman and managing director Tom Johnson.</p>
<p>Philip Kelly, a former director of Ulan Coal Mines Ltd, has been appointed an additional director and deputy chairman.</p>
<p>The company is a steaming coal producer based in the Hunter Valley region of New South Wales, north of Sydney.</p>
<p>Switzerland's Glencore AG is the largest shareholder with a 25.14 percent stake. -- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
